<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     TIME DIFFERENCE MECHANICS SECTION
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Mathematical Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Understanding the 10-Hour PKT to EST Offset</h2>
    <p>
      Converting Pakistan Standard Time to Eastern Standard Time involves a <strong>10-hour subtraction factor</strong> during winter standard time:
    </p>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: bold; color: var(--accent); background: var(--panel); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--line);">
      EST Time = PKT Time − 10 Hours (Winter) <br />
      EDT Time = PKT Time − 9 Hours (Summer)
    </p>
    <p>
      When subtracting 10 hours from early morning times in Pakistan (00:00 to 09:59 PKT), the resulting time falls into the previous calendar day in EST. For instance, 6:00 AM PKT on Wednesday corresponds to 8:00 PM EST on Tuesday evening.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- SIDE-BY-SIDE GRAPHIC -->
  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 700px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 600 180" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="600" height="180" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      
      <g transform="translate(120, 90)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="55" fill="#12455d" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-36" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="25" y2="0" stroke="#8fd7ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <text x="0" y="75" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">PKT (UTC+5)</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(300, 90)">
        <text x="0" y="8" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="28" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">→</text>
        <rect x="-45" y="-30" width="90" height="24" rx="12" fill="#1b536e" />
        <text x="0" y="-14" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="800" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">SUBTRACT 10 HRS</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(480, 90)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="55" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="3" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="-28" y2="-10" stroke="#bdd2dc" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-36" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <text x="0" y="75" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">EST (UTC-5)</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>1. Direct Math Rule</h3>
      <p>Subtract 10 hours from any PKT time. If the value drops below zero, add 24 to find the EST hour and step back one calendar day.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>2. Evening Overlap Window</h3>
      <p>The practical overlap occurs between 6:00 PM and 9:00 PM PKT, which aligns with 8:00 AM to 11:00 AM EST on the US East Coast.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>3. Summer Non-DST Shift</h3>
      <p>Because Pakistan does not observe DST, when New York enters EDT (UTC-4) in spring, subtract 9 hours instead of 10 hours.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

