  <div class="use-cases">
    <article>
      <h3>1. Date Boundary Errors</h3>
      <p>
        Converting PKT hours between 12:00 AM and 9:59 AM shifts the EST time back into the previous calendar evening.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>2. Assuming Pakistan Shifts Clocks</h3>
      <p>
        Pakistan does not use DST. Expecting the offset to remain 10 hours during US summer months leads to 1-hour scheduling errors.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>3. Confusing PKT with IST (India Standard Time)</h3>
      <p>
        India operates at UTC+5:30 (30 minutes ahead of Pakistan). PKT is UTC+5:00. Do not confuse Pakistani and Indian time offsets.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

